{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "Fluids live in a tile's fluid layer (amount 0-8) on top of a non-solid material. ids are persisted in saves: never change or reuse them; 0 means no fluid. kind: liquids fall and fill tiles from the bottom; gases rise, fill the whole tile (amount is concentration) and vanish in open sky. Liquids push gases out of their way. flowEvery: moves on one tick in N (0: never moves). light: emitted at full amount. damagePerSecond applies on 'contact' (any part of the body) or 'breath' (head inside). decay: tiles at or below maxAmount lose one unit every everyTicks ticks (thin gas fades; flames burn out). swimSpeedScale and moveScale scale the player's swim and walk speeds in liquids. Reactions: a tile of `fluid` touching `touching` turns into the material `becomes` or the fluid `becomesFluid`, and removes `consumes` from the touching tile.",
